  "notes": "Glasswater wisp: a pale iris flame spirit about 12x12 (flame tips to base), with a 4 px curling tail below the anchor. The anchor is the flame's base: wisp.rs draws it at the hover height and draws the shadow and the flickering pale iris light itself, so the sheet has no shadow and no painted glow. Non-directional anims named for wisp.rs: idle (flicker loop with a blink), windup (the flame pulls in tall and narrow, the core goes chalk-bright around a face gap that stays dark; stretched over the 38-tick windup), attack (32-tick recoil: burst then cool), hurt (12 ticks: the flame gutters). Flame ramp from palettes_v2.json crystal_violet plus fx.prism #e2d8e9 for the compact core; the darkest step #4d4866 is the rim and is not emissive; the single face gap uses the region outline and never smiles. Eight-way extension: native projected articulated anatomy, unchanged original rows, exact original per-state pose timing and anchors. Source receipts and reproducible geometry tools: art/eightway/glasswater and tools/eightway/glasswater.py.",
  "eightway": {
    "order": [
      "up",
      "up_right",
      "right",
      "down_right",
      "down",
      "down_left",
      "left",
      "up_left"
    ],
    "native_anatomy": true,
    "preserved_source_rows": 4,
    "normal_source": "native articulated geometry; exact same raster as albedo; legacy-first exact-art canonical fields",
    "directionless_effects": [
